  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the time it takes to repair a car. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[2,6],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[2,6],$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(6-2)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{16}{12}=\\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance of the time it takes to repair a car is $\\frac{4}{3}\\,{\\text{hr}}^{2}$",
